1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Hey, Kana! It's time to play!

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Oh! Hi, Saekua!

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Thank you for coming over to play today. I'm glad you're here.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,000
And I'm so glad to be here, Kana!

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
So, uh, are we all alone? Where's your mother?

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
She went out shopping with Lady Toru.

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
So that means it's just the two of us?

8
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Oh, my, my! What do I do?

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Well, am I on my way to becoming a woman?

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Are you okay?

11
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Is this my own Cinderella story?

12
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,000
I think I may need to use your bathroom. Where is it?

13
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Down and to the right.

14
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,000
I got the first time jitters.

15
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Uh, um, excuse me.

16
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,000
The strange girl in the bathroom!

17
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Hey, Lulu. She's a friend.

18
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,000
So it isn't just the two of us after all.

19
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,000
This is the two of us after all.

20
00:02:35,977 --> 00:02:39,637
How long have you known each other?

21
00:02:40,137 --> 00:02:44,257
A while, but she came here recently, and now she lives with us.

22
00:02:44,897 --> 00:02:45,977
She moved in?

23
00:02:49,057 --> 00:02:52,497
Now that I think about it, there are a lot of mysteries around Connor.

24
00:02:52,817 --> 00:02:57,017
She always calls her mother by her last name, and she addresses the maid as lady.

25
00:02:57,577 --> 00:03:01,257
Sometimes I think she's not all there, but then she says something smart.

26
00:03:01,357 --> 00:03:02,597
Psycho-walk.

27
00:03:02,877 --> 00:03:04,337
Are we going to play or not?

28
00:03:05,977 --> 00:03:08,017
Whatever, who cares? She's still cute.

29
00:03:08,537 --> 00:03:11,037
Yeah, I brought some cards with me.

30
00:03:14,477 --> 00:03:17,937
Do you like cards, Alulu?

31
00:03:18,537 --> 00:03:19,517
Want to play with us?

32
00:03:19,617 --> 00:03:20,217
Come play.

33
00:03:21,957 --> 00:03:23,217
No thanks, I'm fine.

34
00:03:28,657 --> 00:03:31,537
I don't get it. Did I say something to upset her?

35
00:03:32,757 --> 00:03:34,237
I lost!

36
00:03:34,237 --> 00:03:36,837
It's too easy. I see it on your face.

37
00:03:37,737 --> 00:03:40,957
I picked the penalty. You must rub my tummy.

38
00:03:40,957 --> 00:03:50,957
This feels more like a reward!

39
00:03:54,717 --> 00:03:59,497
Hey there. I just happened to be in the neighborhood, so I brought you Rugrat some snacks.

40
00:04:00,177 --> 00:04:01,797
Kobayashi and Toru aren't here.

41
00:04:01,877 --> 00:04:04,837
Oh, darn. I guess I'll have to stay and wait for them then.

42
00:04:04,837 --> 00:04:07,057
Meanwhile, split the snacks with your friend here.

43
00:04:07,117 --> 00:04:07,397
Yay!

44
00:04:13,397 --> 00:04:14,237
Hey, kid.

45
00:04:15,517 --> 00:04:16,277
What's wrong?

46
00:04:16,777 --> 00:04:17,997
Why aren't you playing with the others?

47
00:04:17,997 --> 00:04:21,217
I have no right to.

48
00:04:21,217 --> 00:04:25,917
I've been evil. I tried to destroy this city.

49
00:04:27,857 --> 00:04:29,817
I haven't forgiven myself yet.

50
00:04:31,217 --> 00:04:34,597
Then would you like me to turn back time and make it so it never happened?

51
00:04:35,397 --> 00:04:37,317
I could at least do that much for you.

52
00:04:37,317 --> 00:04:41,357
No, it's fine. I know that isn't fair.

53
00:04:42,237 --> 00:04:46,537
Besides, there's something Kobayashi said to me the other day that I can't stop hearing in my head.

54
00:04:47,057 --> 00:04:48,077
Oh, okay, cool.

55
00:04:48,577 --> 00:04:49,837
But no right to play.

56
00:04:50,517 --> 00:04:52,017
Seems a little dramatic to me.

57
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:54,897
I mean, most dragons don't have the right to interact with humans.

58
00:04:55,277 --> 00:04:56,137
Yet, here you are.

59
00:04:56,137 --> 00:05:03,577
It's not working like it did with Miss Kobayashi.

60
00:05:04,557 --> 00:05:07,057
I'll go talk to them for a bit and see what I can do.

61
00:05:08,737 --> 00:05:09,917
Why don't you wait somewhere?

62
00:05:10,517 --> 00:05:11,377
Yeah, there's good.

63
00:05:16,037 --> 00:05:17,797
The truth is, I want to play.

64
00:05:18,137 --> 00:05:20,337
I don't have to lie about those feelings anymore.

65
00:05:20,337 --> 00:05:23,957
But I just don't want them to find out about what I did.

66
00:05:23,957 --> 00:05:27,537
And I don't want anyone to remind Kobayashi.

67
00:05:28,137 --> 00:05:30,477
It seems like she's okay as long as it's resolved.

68
00:05:31,177 --> 00:05:33,317
Oh, I lost again!

69
00:05:34,657 --> 00:05:36,657
Saikawa, are you losing on purpose?

70
00:05:37,197 --> 00:05:39,817
No, not at all! Why would I do that?

71
00:05:40,297 --> 00:05:42,877
Oh, hey, I'm bored playing cards by herself now.

72
00:05:42,877 --> 00:05:45,117
I'm having so much fun with just the two of us!

73
00:05:45,117 --> 00:05:45,837
Meet to pee-bee.

74
00:05:46,357 --> 00:05:47,037
Pee-bee!

75
00:05:51,297 --> 00:05:53,437
I gotta pee. I'll be right back.

76
00:05:53,957 --> 00:05:54,417
Already?

77
00:05:55,557 --> 00:05:58,777
I didn't drink any water. Why do I have to go so much?

78
00:05:59,077 --> 00:05:59,497
Ah!

79
00:06:01,017 --> 00:06:02,917
Um, I'm so sorry!

80
00:06:03,417 --> 00:06:03,817
Ah!

81
00:06:04,357 --> 00:06:06,897
Um, I'm lost, sorta!

82
00:06:07,037 --> 00:06:09,297
So, uh, will you tell me what your name is?

83
00:06:09,557 --> 00:06:11,237
Uh, Saikawa?

84
00:06:12,417 --> 00:06:12,857
Saikawa.

85
00:06:13,537 --> 00:06:16,717
I, um, I actually wanted to play with you earlier.

86
00:06:16,917 --> 00:06:17,157
Huh?

87
00:06:17,157 --> 00:06:20,337
But I didn't think I was allowed to.

88
00:06:20,977 --> 00:06:22,857
I used to be kinda violent.

89
00:06:23,277 --> 00:06:24,437
How were you violent?

90
00:06:25,877 --> 00:06:28,337
I tried to break all sorts of things.

91
00:06:28,337 --> 00:06:31,517
Oh, so a delinquent.

92
00:06:31,517 --> 00:06:34,077
I know what you think.

93
00:06:34,657 --> 00:06:35,857
Violence is bad.

94
00:06:36,797 --> 00:06:37,277
Hmm.

95
00:06:39,117 --> 00:06:42,957
Ah, I'm actually a pretty violent person myself.

96
00:06:43,297 --> 00:06:43,497
Hmm?

97
00:06:43,497 --> 00:06:45,297
You mean that?

98
00:06:45,877 --> 00:06:46,237
Yeah.

99
00:06:46,557 --> 00:06:48,837
I tend to act out when I don't like something.

100
00:06:49,177 --> 00:06:49,437
Uh-huh.

101
00:06:49,817 --> 00:06:52,137
When I first met Kana, I didn't like her at all.

102
00:06:52,317 --> 00:06:54,537
And I thought of many ways to strike her down.

103
00:06:54,777 --> 00:06:55,957
Wow, she's...

104
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:59,377
But, um, she's way too cute to hurt,

105
00:06:59,497 --> 00:07:01,517
so I decided to be friends instead.

106
00:07:02,017 --> 00:07:02,937
She's so...

107
00:07:02,937 --> 00:07:05,077
And to be honest, you're cute, too!

108
00:07:05,817 --> 00:07:07,297
I wanna be your friend, Ilulu!

109
00:07:07,977 --> 00:07:09,677
She's completely lost her mind.

110
00:07:11,017 --> 00:07:13,257
Children that age shouldn't be thinking about

111
00:07:13,257 --> 00:07:16,177
who they can and can't play with based on their pasts.

112
00:07:16,597 --> 00:07:19,157
They're still learning to take responsibility for their faults.

113
00:07:19,897 --> 00:07:22,377
Ilulu never had that opportunity where she's from.

114
00:07:22,917 --> 00:07:25,517
She had to do what she was told or be forced into battle.

115
00:07:25,957 --> 00:07:28,277
She had to be what the adults wanted her to be

116
00:07:28,277 --> 00:07:30,117
if she wanted to fight alongside them.

117
00:07:31,277 --> 00:07:33,697
Thankfully, she can let go of that here.

118
00:07:34,297 --> 00:07:35,977
She has an adult who will be kind to her

119
00:07:35,977 --> 00:07:37,557
and encourage her to be herself.

120
00:07:38,397 --> 00:07:40,877
And if that means being an irresponsible brat

121
00:07:40,877 --> 00:07:43,157
who doesn't know right from wrong, so be it.

122
00:07:55,957 --> 00:08:14,997
We're home!

123
00:08:15,557 --> 00:08:17,377
Hey, Lucoa, I didn't know you were here.

124
00:08:17,757 --> 00:08:18,717
Sorry to make you wait.

125
00:08:18,717 --> 00:08:19,537
We ran into Elma.

126
00:08:21,037 --> 00:08:21,517
Shh.

127
00:08:22,477 --> 00:08:22,677
Hm?

128
00:08:24,677 --> 00:08:25,157
Aw.

129
00:08:27,837 --> 00:08:29,177
Should I wake them up?

130
00:08:29,997 --> 00:08:30,477
No.

131
00:08:31,117 --> 00:08:32,017
Go grab a blanket.

132
00:08:33,077 --> 00:08:34,977
I should probably call Psycho's parents.

133
00:08:34,977 --> 00:08:47,577
I can feel Miss Kobayashi's eyes on my body.

134
00:08:48,057 --> 00:08:49,517
She's staring right through me.

135
00:08:49,797 --> 00:08:52,637
I can feel her passion burning through her side eye.

136
00:08:53,197 --> 00:08:56,317
She's imagining what it would be like to look me all over.

137
00:08:56,457 --> 00:08:57,077
I can tell.

138
00:08:57,297 --> 00:08:59,057
If she doesn't stop, I'll just...

139
00:08:59,057 --> 00:08:59,777
I'll die!

140
00:09:00,257 --> 00:09:01,177
Did you sigh?

141
00:09:01,177 --> 00:09:01,697
Hm?

142
00:09:02,137 --> 00:09:03,357
Yeah, but not about you.

143
00:09:03,937 --> 00:09:05,077
It's that maid outfit.

144
00:09:05,617 --> 00:09:05,917
What?

145
00:09:06,137 --> 00:09:06,737
This one?

146
00:09:07,237 --> 00:09:07,637
Yeah.

147
00:09:08,977 --> 00:09:11,197
I used to have one like it in high school.

148
00:09:11,617 --> 00:09:13,217
I wanted to dress like a maid, too.

149
00:09:13,717 --> 00:09:15,737
Used all the money from my first paycheck.

150
00:09:16,257 --> 00:09:17,817
I wanted to show it off to my family.

151
00:09:18,757 --> 00:09:20,077
And that's when...

152
00:09:20,077 --> 00:09:20,997
What happened?

153
00:09:21,577 --> 00:09:22,917
They said I looked horrible.

154
00:09:24,557 --> 00:09:26,497
Everyone hated it and told me so.

155
00:09:27,337 --> 00:09:29,597
Ever since then, I've embraced being an onlooker.

156
00:09:31,517 --> 00:09:33,957
So, after we had that tragic conversation,

157
00:09:34,277 --> 00:09:36,017
I have come up with a brilliant solution.

158
00:09:36,757 --> 00:09:38,917
We should all design a new style of maid outfit

159
00:09:38,917 --> 00:09:40,397
that would look cute on Miss Kobayashi.

160
00:09:41,157 --> 00:09:43,637
I was hoping I could count on advice from each of you.

161
00:09:45,257 --> 00:09:46,957
It's cute how desperate you become

162
00:09:46,957 --> 00:09:48,897
when you think Miss Kobayashi needs something.

163
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:51,697
It means a lot to me that you could each be here today.

164
00:09:52,077 --> 00:09:52,437
Alma!

165
00:09:52,757 --> 00:09:53,937
What are you doing here?

166
00:09:54,017 --> 00:09:55,117
No one invited you!

167
00:09:55,317 --> 00:09:56,077
That's not true.

168
00:09:56,077 --> 00:09:57,457
Mr. Takya invited me.

169
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:58,977
What the heck is wrong with you?

170
00:09:58,977 --> 00:10:01,617
We were all coming, and I felt bad leaving her out.

171
00:10:01,997 --> 00:10:03,937
It's obvious you felt guilty about it, though.

172
00:10:04,457 --> 00:10:06,797
You mask your embarrassment with displaced anger.

173
00:10:07,077 --> 00:10:07,457
What?

174
00:10:07,637 --> 00:10:08,377
No, I don't!

175
00:10:08,497 --> 00:10:08,917
Shut up!

176
00:10:09,097 --> 00:10:09,677
Oh, hey.

177
00:10:09,917 --> 00:10:11,217
Sorry, I didn't mean to be rude.

178
00:10:11,677 --> 00:10:12,977
I guess we're having a party.

179
00:10:13,237 --> 00:10:14,917
Toru must have planned this while I was napping.

180
00:10:15,757 --> 00:10:17,677
You don't have to be so formal, you know.

181
00:10:18,037 --> 00:10:19,117
We're your friends, too.

182
00:10:19,537 --> 00:10:20,997
And I didn't think it was a party.

183
00:10:21,117 --> 00:10:23,477
I just responded to a friend of mine needing help.

184
00:10:23,697 --> 00:10:24,697
That's so beautiful.

185
00:10:24,697 --> 00:10:27,217
Okay, Georgie, that's enough self-promotion today.

186
00:10:27,497 --> 00:10:28,677
It's time to get started.

187
00:10:28,877 --> 00:10:30,297
Will you please draw your ideas?

188
00:10:30,857 --> 00:10:31,297
Okay.

189
00:10:37,857 --> 00:10:39,477
You're so good at this, Connor.

190
00:10:39,677 --> 00:10:41,997
If you buy one more property, you'll have a monopoly.

191
00:10:43,277 --> 00:10:44,257
A monopoly?

192
00:10:44,977 --> 00:10:46,877
Yeah, it means you're like the king of it.

193
00:10:46,977 --> 00:10:49,517
You'll be able to do whatever you want with all the spaces.

194
00:10:49,517 --> 00:10:55,977
Why don't you place a house in Connor's area?

195
00:10:56,837 --> 00:10:59,077
Sorry about it, but this is a competition.

196
00:11:00,537 --> 00:11:02,257
I don't really understand the rules,

197
00:11:02,377 --> 00:11:04,617
but this game seems to bring out the worst in all of them.

198
00:11:05,877 --> 00:11:06,277
Done.

199
00:11:06,617 --> 00:11:07,657
That was fast.

200
00:11:07,837 --> 00:11:08,377
Let's see.

201
00:11:08,577 --> 00:11:09,837
When Miss Kobayashi's at work,

202
00:11:09,917 --> 00:11:12,617
she's always so stoic and gets everything done as soon as possible.

203
00:11:12,917 --> 00:11:14,237
So I came up with this.

204
00:11:14,717 --> 00:11:17,457
What does your obsession with dessert have to do with any of this?

205
00:11:17,457 --> 00:11:19,797
What? It's symbolic.

206
00:11:20,197 --> 00:11:22,597
It's my favorite meal, and it makes me feel secure.

207
00:11:23,637 --> 00:11:26,177
Will you please go play with the children in the other room?

208
00:11:26,217 --> 00:11:27,337
I can't handle you.

209
00:11:27,637 --> 00:11:29,177
Okay, see what you think of this one.

210
00:11:30,757 --> 00:11:33,337
I mean, it's cute, but, like, too cute,

211
00:11:33,397 --> 00:11:34,717
as in it won't look good on me.

212
00:11:36,137 --> 00:11:36,837
That's awkward.

213
00:11:36,977 --> 00:11:39,237
We're supposed to draw one with the idea you would wear it?

214
00:11:39,437 --> 00:11:39,837
Kinda.

215
00:11:41,637 --> 00:11:42,657
I'm done, too.

216
00:11:43,497 --> 00:11:44,417
Where's the top?

217
00:11:44,497 --> 00:11:44,917
I don't know.

218
00:11:44,917 --> 00:11:47,357
Our local servants never complained when they had them on.

219
00:11:47,457 --> 00:11:49,197
I'm too pasty to wear this.

220
00:11:49,457 --> 00:11:50,117
Mine's done.

221
00:11:50,997 --> 00:11:51,857
Okay, let's see.

222
00:11:52,457 --> 00:11:53,457
Oh, thank goodness.

223
00:11:53,917 --> 00:11:55,417
She's the one I'm counting on.

224
00:11:55,817 --> 00:11:57,257
Here, see what you think.

225
00:11:57,417 --> 00:11:58,357
Oh, thanks.

226
00:11:59,477 --> 00:12:02,977
I went with the longer dress style and very minimal adornments.

227
00:12:03,197 --> 00:12:05,837
She's serving classic refinement with small-town simplicity.

228
00:12:06,277 --> 00:12:08,737
If I remember correctly, that's your type, isn't it?

229
00:12:08,857 --> 00:12:10,097
Yeah, it is.

230
00:12:10,097 --> 00:12:13,777
However, we really can't define one maid outfit.

231
00:12:14,477 --> 00:12:16,857
Though styles change with different eras,

232
00:12:17,017 --> 00:12:19,037
the design becomes more polished every day

233
00:12:19,037 --> 00:12:21,857
as the maid herself evolves in preferences and customs.

234
00:12:22,657 --> 00:12:26,117
What's consistent is that it's always a maid who wears it.

235
00:12:26,637 --> 00:12:29,577
It's her talent and skill that qualifies one as a maid,

236
00:12:29,657 --> 00:12:30,537
not what she wears.

237
00:12:30,537 --> 00:12:33,717
The maid outfit is called that

238
00:12:33,717 --> 00:12:35,497
because a maid decided to wear it.

239
00:12:37,357 --> 00:12:40,357
Miss Kobayashi, I am also a student.

240
00:12:41,397 --> 00:12:44,157
It would be inappropriate for me to wear my maid outfit to school

241
00:12:44,157 --> 00:12:45,517
or out with friends, wouldn't it?

242
00:12:46,077 --> 00:12:48,117
However, just because I'm not wearing it

243
00:12:48,117 --> 00:12:49,257
doesn't mean I'm not a maid.

244
00:12:49,637 --> 00:12:51,397
Even if I'm wearing my school uniform,

245
00:12:51,557 --> 00:12:53,577
I'm still a maid, but in a different place.

246
00:12:54,217 --> 00:12:57,177
Therefore, a school uniform can actually become a maid outfit.

247
00:12:57,177 --> 00:13:00,717
So, it's not what we wear.

248
00:13:01,217 --> 00:13:02,577
It's what's in our hearts.

249
00:13:02,597 --> 00:13:04,077
It's the spirit of service.

250
00:13:05,897 --> 00:13:07,457
Quit changing the subject!

251
00:13:07,997 --> 00:13:08,697
Hey, Toru.

252
00:13:09,077 --> 00:13:10,557
You weren't supposed to come back.

253
00:13:10,937 --> 00:13:12,177
We just finished a round.

254
00:13:12,717 --> 00:13:13,677
But I'm curious.

255
00:13:14,097 --> 00:13:15,777
You've been criticizing our designs.

256
00:13:16,097 --> 00:13:17,597
I want to see what you came up with.

257
00:13:18,177 --> 00:13:19,357
Yeah, okay, later.

258
00:13:19,677 --> 00:13:21,217
That's not suspicious or anything.

259
00:13:21,357 --> 00:13:22,897
Let me take off of me, you better!

260
00:13:24,897 --> 00:13:25,337
Huh?

261
00:13:25,337 --> 00:13:27,397
Toru, it's completely blank.

262
00:13:27,697 --> 00:13:28,677
You couldn't think of anything?

263
00:13:30,837 --> 00:13:32,037
It's not that.

264
00:13:32,757 --> 00:13:35,117
I was just thinking I'd really like Miss Kobayashi

265
00:13:35,117 --> 00:13:36,357
to wear my maid outfit.

266
00:13:40,537 --> 00:13:42,017
There's no way I could do that.

267
00:13:42,237 --> 00:13:43,817
Your outfit is too adorable for me.

268
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:45,597
Oh, okay.

269
00:13:47,037 --> 00:13:48,257
But sure, why not?

270
00:13:48,257 --> 00:13:51,417
I mean, you did go out of your way

271
00:13:51,417 --> 00:13:53,657
to arrange this maid fashion focus group for me.

272
00:13:53,657 --> 00:13:55,337
I'll do it.

273
00:13:56,137 --> 00:13:57,597
Do you really mean that?

274
00:13:58,937 --> 00:13:59,877
Okay, there.

275
00:14:00,257 --> 00:14:01,237
I'm wearing it.

276
00:14:01,857 --> 00:14:02,217
Oh!

277
00:14:04,337 --> 00:14:05,677
You look so good!

278
00:14:05,897 --> 00:14:07,357
That one looks great on you.

279
00:14:07,737 --> 00:14:08,757
Please, stop.

280
00:14:08,997 --> 00:14:10,177
Enough with the flattery.

281
00:14:10,217 --> 00:14:11,437
I don't know how to handle it.

282
00:14:11,477 --> 00:14:12,797
Let's take a photo together!

283
00:14:13,077 --> 00:14:14,777
Me and you in matching maid garb.

284
00:14:14,897 --> 00:14:16,517
We're like maid to Lindsay's.

285
00:14:16,517 --> 00:14:19,517
If we're taking a photo, then everyone should be in it.

286
00:14:19,517 --> 00:14:19,957
Ugh!

287
00:14:20,957 --> 00:14:21,397
Fine!

288
00:14:21,557 --> 00:14:22,437
Come on, everyone!

289
00:14:22,697 --> 00:14:23,197
Get in here!

290
00:14:23,217 --> 00:14:25,257
I get to be next to Miss Kobayashi!

291
00:14:25,257 --> 00:14:26,477
Oh, that's not fair!

292
00:14:26,517 --> 00:14:29,277
It was my idea to take it, and I was here first!

293
00:14:31,377 --> 00:14:32,277
Hey, Toru?

294
00:14:32,717 --> 00:14:33,037
Yes?

295
00:14:33,897 --> 00:14:35,937
There's something I realized today.

296
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:37,697
And what might that be?

297
00:14:37,697 --> 00:14:39,357
You remember what Georgie said?

298
00:14:39,797 --> 00:14:40,537
The maid sermon?

299
00:14:41,057 --> 00:14:41,477
Oh, yeah.

300
00:14:42,217 --> 00:14:44,637
It's only a maid outfit because a maid wears it.

301
00:14:45,057 --> 00:14:49,677
That also means, if someone wears the exact same outfit, but they're not really a maid,

302
00:14:50,017 --> 00:14:51,357
then they're just a cosplayer.

303
00:14:52,357 --> 00:14:56,617
Your uniform always bothered me, but after wearing it today, I had a change of heart,

304
00:14:56,757 --> 00:14:58,137
embarrassing though it was.

305
00:14:58,137 --> 00:15:00,817
It wasn't horrifying.

306
00:15:02,077 --> 00:15:05,317
I've always liked that style and wondered what it would be like to wear one.

307
00:15:06,397 --> 00:15:10,397
But I didn't think I was cute or girly enough, so I wore men's clothes instead.

308
00:15:11,397 --> 00:15:14,117
I was afraid others would laugh if I wore a dress or something.

309
00:15:14,997 --> 00:15:18,677
Well, now I realize that if I wanted to wear a maid outfit, I should have just worn it.

310
00:15:19,037 --> 00:15:20,477
And that showed me another reality.

311
00:15:21,297 --> 00:15:23,837
I wanted to be the cosplayer I always mocked.

312
00:15:24,477 --> 00:15:27,297
But I could never make myself look as hot as the rest of them.

313
00:15:27,297 --> 00:15:33,337
So I became an annoying maid otaku instead and obsessed about refinement and historical accuracy.

314
00:15:33,877 --> 00:15:34,997
Miss Kobayashi.

315
00:15:36,377 --> 00:15:37,497
I get it now.

316
00:15:38,037 --> 00:15:38,917
I see you.

317
00:15:39,337 --> 00:15:41,897
You work hard every day to serve as the perfect maid.

318
00:15:42,597 --> 00:15:44,357
I'm sorry I called you a cosplayer.

319
00:15:44,537 --> 00:15:47,497
Anything you wear can only be defined as true maid attire.

320
00:15:49,477 --> 00:15:52,657
Took you long enough to realize, but at least you're being genuine.

321
00:15:53,117 --> 00:15:55,837
Luckily, I still love you when you're unfair and unreasonable.

322
00:15:55,837 --> 00:15:59,337
You know, I never could have said these things to you when you first came here.

323
00:15:59,417 --> 00:16:00,697
Give me some credit, at least.

324
00:16:01,497 --> 00:16:04,037
I appreciate everything you do around the house, Toru.

325
00:16:04,217 --> 00:16:04,817
Thank you.

326
00:16:05,257 --> 00:16:06,377
Me, Toru!

327
00:16:06,497 --> 00:16:08,377
Why is that so hard for you to say?

328
00:16:08,377 --> 00:16:15,257
Hey, this is the last bill I have.

329
00:16:15,337 --> 00:16:17,237
Alolu, you're not very good with money.

330
00:16:17,557 --> 00:16:18,577
Don't worry about it.

331
00:16:19,037 --> 00:16:20,937
I'm sure you'll pass the bank pretty soon.

332
00:16:21,317 --> 00:16:23,477
And that's when you'll get some of your money back.

333
00:16:23,577 --> 00:16:24,597
Okay, that's good.

334
00:16:25,177 --> 00:16:28,197
But still, Shota Street is right after that.

335
00:16:28,737 --> 00:16:32,197
So no matter where I stop, I'll still have to pay expensive rental fees.

336
00:16:32,197 --> 00:16:35,477
There's no need to be nervous if you know what to expect.

337
00:16:36,217 --> 00:16:37,537
Shut up, Root Demon!

338
00:16:39,277 --> 00:16:40,957
Alolu looks chapped out.

339
00:16:42,397 --> 00:16:44,217
Can you tell me if you have any hobbies?

340
00:16:44,677 --> 00:16:45,977
I like being a maid.

341
00:16:46,397 --> 00:16:47,757
Does that make it a hobby?

342
00:16:48,057 --> 00:16:51,417
As far as free time, I have a lot of it.

343
00:16:53,097 --> 00:16:54,897
What are your hobbies, Misasaki Bay?

344
00:16:55,397 --> 00:16:58,097
Lately, I've been into making all kinds of delicious sweets.

345
00:16:58,097 --> 00:17:00,597
Is that what that piercing noise was earlier?

346
00:17:01,297 --> 00:17:02,797
Oh, I'm so sorry.

347
00:17:02,957 --> 00:17:03,717
Was it that loud?

348
00:17:04,797 --> 00:17:05,577
Well, darn.

349
00:17:06,097 --> 00:17:07,477
I still can't think of anything.

350
00:17:08,637 --> 00:17:09,897
I used to love traveling.

351
00:17:10,017 --> 00:17:11,097
I wonder if that would count.

352
00:17:12,657 --> 00:17:13,517
Maybe music?

353
00:17:14,457 --> 00:17:16,717
That's something that's popular among the humans.

354
00:17:18,257 --> 00:17:20,857
Speaking of music, there's nihilistic Mr. Yana.

355
00:17:21,337 --> 00:17:23,017
You said you wanted to ask me a question?

356
00:17:23,277 --> 00:17:23,737
What is it?

357
00:17:24,197 --> 00:17:26,417
I want to know what you find fun about music.

358
00:17:26,417 --> 00:17:28,837
Probably the way it lights a fire in your soul

359
00:17:28,837 --> 00:17:30,057
and makes your heart go bummer.

360
00:17:30,657 --> 00:17:32,237
Makes your heart go bummer?

361
00:17:33,117 --> 00:17:34,577
Go ahead and give it a try

362
00:17:34,577 --> 00:17:36,197
and then I'll teach you some simple chords.

363
00:17:36,477 --> 00:17:36,737
Okay.

364
00:17:46,597 --> 00:17:48,677
I'm confused as to how it works.

365
00:17:49,157 --> 00:17:50,637
What? Is there something wrong?

366
00:17:50,797 --> 00:17:51,377
It hurts.

367
00:17:51,717 --> 00:17:52,857
Your talent is so brutal.

368
00:17:53,517 --> 00:17:55,057
I didn't mean to depress him.

369
00:17:55,057 --> 00:17:56,537
Hi, Mr. Sone.

370
00:17:57,257 --> 00:17:58,677
I just finished this one

371
00:17:58,677 --> 00:18:00,457
and thought you might have a shelf to put it on.

372
00:18:00,597 --> 00:18:00,977
Wow.

373
00:18:01,257 --> 00:18:03,077
It came out exactly as good as the last.

374
00:18:03,417 --> 00:18:04,497
You must have a lot of fun

375
00:18:04,497 --> 00:18:05,977
making stuff like this, don't you?

376
00:18:06,637 --> 00:18:07,777
Would you like to try one?

377
00:18:10,177 --> 00:18:11,017
What do you think?

378
00:18:12,217 --> 00:18:12,957
Let's see.

379
00:18:13,757 --> 00:18:16,397
It is an incredibly elaborate design.

380
00:18:16,757 --> 00:18:18,157
There aren't many who could make something

381
00:18:18,157 --> 00:18:19,697
this advanced on their first try.

382
00:18:19,697 --> 00:18:21,397
Thanks, but I still don't understand

383
00:18:21,397 --> 00:18:22,737
what you find fun about it.

384
00:18:23,177 --> 00:18:24,937
I tried playing some music too,

385
00:18:25,037 --> 00:18:26,037
but I wasn't amused.

386
00:18:26,417 --> 00:18:27,697
You know, I'm fairly certain

387
00:18:27,697 --> 00:18:28,757
I happened to hear that.

388
00:18:29,257 --> 00:18:30,297
It sounded to me like

389
00:18:30,297 --> 00:18:32,157
you were just focusing on playing the notes

390
00:18:32,157 --> 00:18:34,017
instead of making it your own.

391
00:18:34,377 --> 00:18:36,077
So you could tell just by listening?

392
00:18:36,077 --> 00:18:38,497
Sounded like it was too easy for you.

393
00:18:38,737 --> 00:18:40,197
There was no challenge to overcome,

394
00:18:40,417 --> 00:18:41,677
so no emotion was invested.

395
00:18:42,297 --> 00:18:44,737
Without curiosity and emotional investment,

396
00:18:45,237 --> 00:18:47,097
the hobby you choose won't be fulfilling.

397
00:18:47,957 --> 00:18:50,437
Oh, is that how a hobby's supposed to work?

398
00:18:51,157 --> 00:18:52,157
I'm back.

399
00:18:52,277 --> 00:18:53,157
Welcome home, Kana.

400
00:18:55,277 --> 00:18:57,317
Would you say that you have any hobbies?

401
00:18:58,277 --> 00:18:58,937
Yeah, duh.

402
00:18:58,937 --> 00:19:01,777
I like to walk on this white line.

403
00:19:02,157 --> 00:19:04,257
How are you emotionally invested in this?

404
00:19:04,337 --> 00:19:05,697
If I fall, I die.

405
00:19:06,777 --> 00:19:07,997
I see now.

406
00:19:08,257 --> 00:19:10,557
This helps her prepare for battle in limited spaces.

407
00:19:11,037 --> 00:19:12,557
I did not take Kana's instincts

408
00:19:12,557 --> 00:19:14,217
as a dragon seriously enough.

409
00:19:14,617 --> 00:19:15,737
Oh, it stopped.

410
00:19:18,837 --> 00:19:19,937
Let's keep going.

411
00:19:20,417 --> 00:19:21,057
It's cool.

412
00:19:21,157 --> 00:19:22,077
I'm over it now.

413
00:19:23,037 --> 00:19:26,437
I mean, aren't hobbies at least supposed to be fun?

414
00:19:26,557 --> 00:19:28,437
I have fun when I do it with Saikawa.

415
00:19:28,937 --> 00:19:30,677
Hello, and welcome home, you two.

416
00:19:31,657 --> 00:19:32,517
No fair.

417
00:19:32,697 --> 00:19:33,837
Can I have one of those donuts?

418
00:19:34,477 --> 00:19:35,377
Go away.

419
00:19:35,857 --> 00:19:36,917
Please help me.

420
00:19:37,157 --> 00:19:38,797
All you do is sleep for days.

421
00:19:39,137 --> 00:19:40,457
If you don't work, then you don't eat.

422
00:19:40,697 --> 00:19:41,337
Them's the rules.

423
00:19:42,137 --> 00:19:43,817
How come you don't have any hobbies, Yilulu?

424
00:19:44,737 --> 00:19:45,317
I do.

425
00:19:45,697 --> 00:19:46,957
I'm very good at sleeping.

426
00:19:47,477 --> 00:19:48,377
That's not a hobby.

427
00:19:48,477 --> 00:19:49,637
That's your lifestyle choice.

428
00:19:49,897 --> 00:19:50,997
Why are you so mean?

429
00:19:51,837 --> 00:19:52,237
Me?

430
00:19:52,237 --> 00:19:52,637
Me?

431
00:19:54,437 --> 00:19:55,837
What flavor is it?

432
00:19:55,857 --> 00:19:58,237
Seems like finding a hobby is hard.

433
00:19:59,137 --> 00:20:01,417
Some of the kids at school like to be idols.

434
00:20:01,697 --> 00:20:03,097
I heard something about that.

435
00:20:03,477 --> 00:20:06,037
I'm not into singing or getting that much attention.

436
00:20:06,437 --> 00:20:06,637
Ow.

437
00:20:09,437 --> 00:20:10,317
I know.

438
00:20:10,597 --> 00:20:11,237
That's it.

439
00:20:11,237 --> 00:20:21,857
I'll get Ms. Kobayashi to become a famous idol.

440
00:20:22,517 --> 00:20:24,117
We're the two.

441
00:20:27,117 --> 00:20:28,177
Good work today.

442
00:20:28,437 --> 00:20:29,157
Yeah, you too.

443
00:20:30,017 --> 00:20:31,077
Hey, Kana, what's up?

444
00:20:31,297 --> 00:20:32,637
Please come home right away.

445
00:20:32,977 --> 00:20:34,917
Lady Toru's completely lost it.

446
00:20:35,177 --> 00:20:35,957
She what?

447
00:20:35,957 --> 00:20:37,197
What's going on?

448
00:20:37,257 --> 00:20:42,277
Love kids, love kids, love kids, love kids, I love this Kobayashi.

449
00:20:43,917 --> 00:20:49,517
Love kids, love kids, love kids, love kids, I love this Kobayashi, yeah.

450
00:20:50,677 --> 00:20:51,937
Love the kids.

451
00:20:51,937 --> 00:20:54,297
What the?

452
00:20:55,077 --> 00:20:59,297
She keeps making Kobayashi merch and forcing us to like them.

453
00:20:59,377 --> 00:21:01,877
She also just won't stop singing songs about you.

454
00:21:02,517 --> 00:21:05,117
Kobayashi, having hobbies is so much fun.

455
00:21:05,237 --> 00:21:10,517
Uh, my drinking hobby makes me act the same way, so I got nothing.

456
00:21:10,517 --> 00:21:18,177
I've made the target earnings, now I just need to reach the goal.

457
00:21:19,317 --> 00:21:21,437
Psycho, what are we supposed to do?

458
00:21:28,697 --> 00:21:29,617
No way!

459
00:21:29,737 --> 00:21:31,277
That's my Katawana!

460
00:21:31,617 --> 00:21:32,697
How'd you do that?

461
00:21:33,657 --> 00:21:37,057
I made a wise investment and transferred all my assets over to Kana.

462
00:21:37,517 --> 00:21:39,057
You can't do that, that's cheating!

463
00:21:39,057 --> 00:21:41,617
I've already given her everything else I have!

464
00:21:41,817 --> 00:21:43,777
My heart, my soul, and my body!

465
00:21:43,937 --> 00:21:44,297
Ah!

466
00:21:44,497 --> 00:21:45,677
My beloved king!

467
00:21:45,737 --> 00:21:47,097
Worship me, human.

468
00:21:47,717 --> 00:21:48,237
Ah!

469
00:23:19,887 --> 00:23:24,067
What's your hobby, Lucoa?

470
00:23:24,847 --> 00:23:25,947
Shota, baby.

471
00:23:26,307 --> 00:23:28,887
I figured. And yours is games, right, Bafnir?

472
00:23:29,067 --> 00:23:29,467
Wrong.

473
00:23:29,607 --> 00:23:30,547
What? It's not?

474
00:23:30,747 --> 00:23:31,047
No.

475
00:23:31,447 --> 00:23:32,247
Since when?

476
00:23:32,487 --> 00:23:33,007
None, yeah.

477
00:23:36,187 --> 00:23:38,487
This week on Who's Rotten?

478
00:23:39,587 --> 00:23:40,147
Sagittarius.

